<title>FRANCE: Valeo shares rise after results.</title>
<headline>Valeo shares rise after results.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-09-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in car parts manufacturer Valeo rose on Friday after several brokers raised their rating following a 31 percent jump in the company's pre-exceptional first-half profit.</p>
<p>CDC Bourse switched to buy from neutral, Paribas Capital Markets to hold from sell and Cheuvreux de Virieu to buy from sell, traders said.</p>
<p>The share was 17.5 francs higher at 280 at 1415 GMT.</p>
<p>&quot;Their results were really good,&quot; a broker said, adding that buyout speculation appeared to have revived in recent days.</p>
<p>-- Paris Newsroom, +33 1 4221 5452</p>
